Tailspin Toys is building a custom synced Copilot connector for its ticketing system by using Microsoft Graph PowerShell. You have the following requirements:

- The ticketTitle property must be shown as the item title in Microsoft 365 experiences.
- Users must be able to query tickets by the priority property by name, for example priority:High.
- The schema must be registered on an existing connection.

How should you complete the script? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.

```powershell
$params = @{
  baseType = "microsoft.graph.externalItem"
  properties = @(
    @{ name = "ticketTitle"; type = "String"; isSearchable = "true"; isRetrievable = "true"; labels = @("[[1]]") }
    @{ name = "priority"; type = "String"; [[2]] = "true"; isRetrievable = "true" }
  )
}
[[3]] -ExternalConnectionId $connectionId -BodyParameter $params
```
